From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sunxi: h713-r: the header names the EINT function as fn14, as the table has it

0140 moved every R_PIO pin's interrupt function from mux 0x6 to 0xe
(SUNXI_FUNCTION_IRQ_BANK(0xe, ...)), the value the stock kernel's
SUNXI_PCTL_HW_TYPE_1 tables carry and the one that raised EINT4 for the
power key on the HY310 (09.09.2026). The comment block at the top of the
file still listed "PL_EINTn (fn6)" for all sixteen PL pins and the PM
bank, the H616 value that disconnects the input on this SoC. Comments
only; no table entry, no register write changes.

The same correction is in cstenger's 0171 (commit 73ee74a, 07.10.2026),
which also notes that the other alternate functions in this comment
disagree with stock in places (PL4: s_twi1 fn2, s_jtag0 fn3). Those are
left as they are here: not checked against our own dumps.

Signed-off-by: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun50i-h713-r.c | 37 ++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun50i-h713-r.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun50i-h713-r.c
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun50i-h713-r.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun50i-h713-r.c
@@ -15,26 +15,27 @@
  * - Live register dumps from HY310 hardware
  * - Comparison with H6 R_PIO (similar architecture)
  *
- * PL bank functions (from stock DTS + register analysis):
- *   PL0:  gpio, s_rsb_scl/s_twi_scl (fn2/fn3), PL_EINT0 (fn6)
- *   PL1:  gpio, s_rsb_sda/s_twi_sda (fn2/fn3), PL_EINT1 (fn6)
- *   PL2:  gpio, s_uart_tx (fn2), PL_EINT2 (fn6)
- *   PL3:  gpio, s_uart_rx (fn2), PL_EINT3 (fn6)
- *   PL4:  gpio, s_jtag_ms (fn2), PL_EINT4 (fn6)
- *   PL5:  gpio, s_jtag_ck (fn2), PL_EINT5 (fn6)
- *   PL6:  gpio, s_pwm0 (fn2), s_jtag_do (fn3), PL_EINT6 (fn6)
- *   PL7:  gpio, s_pwm1 (fn2), s_jtag_di (fn3), PL_EINT7 (fn6)
- *   PL8:  gpio, s_pwm2 (fn2), PL_EINT8 (fn6)
- *   PL9:  gpio, s_cir (fn3), PL_EINT9 (fn6)
- *   PL10: gpio, s_twi0_scl (fn2), PL_EINT10 (fn6)
- *   PL11: gpio, s_twi0_sda (fn2), PL_EINT11 (fn6)
- *   PL12: gpio, s_twi1_scl (fn2), PL_EINT12 (fn6)
- *   PL13: gpio, s_twi1_sda (fn2), PL_EINT13 (fn6)
- *   PL14: gpio, s_twi2_scl (fn2), PL_EINT14 (fn6)
- *   PL15: gpio, s_twi2_sda (fn2), PL_EINT15 (fn6)
+ * PL bank functions (from stock DTS + register analysis; the EINT function is
+ * mux 0xe = fn14, as the table below has it since 0140):
+ *   PL0:  gpio, s_rsb_scl/s_twi_scl (fn2/fn3), PL_EINT0 (fn14)
+ *   PL1:  gpio, s_rsb_sda/s_twi_sda (fn2/fn3), PL_EINT1 (fn14)
+ *   PL2:  gpio, s_uart_tx (fn2), PL_EINT2 (fn14)
+ *   PL3:  gpio, s_uart_rx (fn2), PL_EINT3 (fn14)
+ *   PL4:  gpio, s_jtag_ms (fn2), PL_EINT4 (fn14)
+ *   PL5:  gpio, s_jtag_ck (fn2), PL_EINT5 (fn14)
+ *   PL6:  gpio, s_pwm0 (fn2), s_jtag_do (fn3), PL_EINT6 (fn14)
+ *   PL7:  gpio, s_pwm1 (fn2), s_jtag_di (fn3), PL_EINT7 (fn14)
+ *   PL8:  gpio, s_pwm2 (fn2), PL_EINT8 (fn14)
+ *   PL9:  gpio, s_cir (fn3), PL_EINT9 (fn14)
+ *   PL10: gpio, s_twi0_scl (fn2), PL_EINT10 (fn14)
+ *   PL11: gpio, s_twi0_sda (fn2), PL_EINT11 (fn14)
+ *   PL12: gpio, s_twi1_scl (fn2), PL_EINT12 (fn14)
+ *   PL13: gpio, s_twi1_sda (fn2), PL_EINT13 (fn14)
+ *   PL14: gpio, s_twi2_scl (fn2), PL_EINT14 (fn14)
+ *   PL15: gpio, s_twi2_sda (fn2), PL_EINT15 (fn14)
  *
  * PM bank functions (from stock DTS GPIO references):
- *   PM0-PM4: gpio, PL_EINT (fn6) — used for WLAN/BT control
+ *   PM0-PM4: gpio, PL_EINT (fn14) — used for WLAN/BT control
  */
 
 #include <linux/init.h>
